    "congress": 118,
    "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 170, Number 30 (Thursday, February 15, 2024)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"https://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Mr. TAKANO:\nH.R. 7394.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle I Section 8\nThe single subject of this legislation is:\nEnsure defendants have access to source code and other\ninformation necessary to exercise their confrontational and\ndue process rights when algorithms are used to analyze\nevidence in their cases.\n[Page H680]\n</pre>",
